course: dictionary
lesson: 3687
title: Flammable and warning labels
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Flammable means something catches fire easily and burns quickly. You can work this out from the context. «Alcohol hand gel is flammable and must not be swallowed.» The warning that it must not be swallowed tells you it is dangerous, and flammable is the clue that it can catch fire.
explain: Labels give clues too. A flame symbol shows that a product is flammable. «Keep away from fire» and «highly flammable» are warnings to stay well away from heat and flames.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «Chemicals stay safe when they stay in their own labelled bottles, locked or up high.» Put in "easily set on fire" for flammable, and the warning still makes sense: keep these bottles away from anything that could start a fire.
fact: Flammable means easily set on fire and burning quickly.
fact: A flame symbol on a label shows that something is flammable.
fact: Flammable materials include paper, petrol, some gases, aerosol cans and some clothes.
fact: «Highly flammable» means it catches fire very easily.
fact: «Flammable liquid» is a warning that the liquid can catch fire.
exercise: «Keep away from fire», «highly flammable». What does flammable mean? | *Easily set on fire and burning quickly | Good for cooking food | Very cold to touch | Safe to swallow
exercise: Which label warns you that a product can catch fire easily? | A snowflake | A picture of a rainbow | A smiling face | *A flame symbol
exercise: Which of these is flammable? | A stone | Water | *Petrol | A glass bottle
test: «Alcohol hand gel is flammable and must not be swallowed.» In this sentence, flammable means | *It can catch fire easily | It is good for drinking | It is sweet to taste | It cleans dirt very slowly
test: Warning symbols show if a product is corrosive, toxic, flammable or harmful. Which word means poisonous? | corrosive | harmful | *toxic | flammable
exam: Mia reads «flammable liquid» on a bottle. What should she do? | Light it to see what happens | Drink a little to check it | Leave it next to the cooker | *Keep it away from flames and heat
